== 3.8 Chapter 3 Practice Drill — 30 Questions

30 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 33 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [A cell with 24 chromosomes divides by mitosis. Each daughter cell will contain],
  [48 chromosomes],
  [12 chromosomes],
  [24 chromosomes],
  [6 chromosomes]
)

#mcq(2, [Crossing over takes place during],
  [metaphase of mitosis],
  [prophase I of meiosis],
  [anaphase II of meiosis],
  [telophase of mitosis]
)

#mcq(3, [Meiosis in a human male produces],
  [two cells with 46 chromosomes],
  [four cells with 46 chromosomes],
  [two cells with 23 chromosomes],
  [four cells with 23 chromosomes]
)

#mcq(4, [The stage at which chromosomes line up at the equator is],
  [telophase],
  [prophase],
  [metaphase],
  [anaphase]
)

#mcq(5, [DNA replication occurs during],
  [telophase],
  [anaphase],
  [interphase],
  [prophase]
)

#mcq(6, [The number of chromosomes in each cell produced by meiosis compared with the parent cell is],
  [the same],
  [trebled],
  [halved],
  [doubled]
)

#mcq(7, [Which of these occurs in meiosis but not in mitosis?],
  [Separation of chromatids],
  [Crossing over and formation of four haploid cells],
  [Formation of spindle fibres],
  [Chromosome replication]
)

#mcq(8, [Mitosis is important in],
  [growth and repair of body tissues],
  [the halving of chromosome number],
  [the formation of gametes],
  [the production of variation]
)

#mcq(9, [The centromere is the region of a chromosome that],
  [contains the genes],
  [joins the two chromatids and attaches to the spindle],
  [is lost during division],
  [codes for protein]
)

#mcq(10, [After fertilisation, the human zygote contains],
  [92 chromosomes],
  [12 chromosomes],
  [23 chromosomes],
  [46 chromosomes]
)

#mcq(11, [A cell with a diploid number of 8 undergoes meiosis. The number of chromosomes in each gamete is],
  [2],
  [16],
  [8],
  [4]
)

#mcq(12, [Which process increases genetic variation?],
  [Meiosis and random fertilisation],
  [Binary fission],
  [Mitosis only],
  [DNA replication alone]
)

#mcq(13, [Cytokinesis is the division of the],
  [chromosomes],
  [nucleus],
  [cytoplasm],
  [cell wall]
)

#mcq(14, [During anaphase of mitosis],
  [chromatids separate and move to opposite poles],
  [the nuclear membrane reforms],
  [the cell plate forms],
  [chromosomes line up at the equator]
)

#mcq(15, [Cancer may be described as a failure of],
  [respiration],
  [digestion],
  [photosynthesis],
  [control of cell division]
)

#mcq(16, [Which of these produces four genetically different cells?],
  [Budding],
  [Meiosis],
  [Mitosis],
  [Binary fission]
)

#mcq(17, [In a flowering plant, meiosis occurs in the],
  [leaf mesophyll],
  [anther and ovary],
  [root tip],
  [shoot tip]
)

