=== Complete Solutions

#sol-item(1, "C", dense: true)[
  Mitosis conserves the chromosome number, so each daughter receives the same 24 as the parent.
]

#sol-item(2, "B", dense: true)[
  Homologous chromosomes pair and exchange segments in prophase I of meiosis.
]

#sol-item(3, "D", dense: true)[
  Two divisions produce four haploid gametes, each with 23 chromosomes.
]

#sol-item(4, "C", dense: true)[
  Metaphase — chromosomes at the equator, spindle fibres attached to centromeres.
]

#sol-item(5, "C", dense: true)[
  The DNA is copied in interphase, before mitosis begins.
]

#sol-item(6, "C", dense: true)[
  Meiosis is the reduction division: $2n$ becomes $n$.
]

#sol-item(7, "B", dense: true)[
  Crossing over and the halving of the chromosome number are unique to meiosis.
]

#sol-item(8, "A", dense: true)[
  Mitosis makes identical body cells for growth, repair and asexual reproduction.
]

#sol-item(9, "B", dense: true)[
  The centromere holds the sister chromatids together and is the attachment point for spindle fibres.
]

#sol-item(10, "D", dense: true)[
  Two haploid gametes fuse: 23 + 23 = 46.
]

#sol-item(11, "D", dense: true)[
  Meiosis halves the number, so 8 becomes 4.
]

#sol-item(12, "A", dense: true)[
  Crossing over, independent assortment in meiosis, and random fertilisation all increase variation.
]

#sol-item(13, "C", dense: true)[
  Karyokinesis divides the nucleus; cytokinesis divides the cytoplasm.
]

#sol-item(14, "A", dense: true)[
  Anaphase is the movement of chromatids away from each other towards the poles.
]

#sol-item(15, "D", dense: true)[
  Uncontrolled division follows damage to the genes that regulate the cell cycle.
]

#sol-item(16, "B", dense: true)[
  Only meiosis produces four cells, each genetically different from the others.
]

#sol-item(17, "B", dense: true)[
  Gametes are formed in the anther (pollen) and ovary (ovules), the plant's reproductive organs.
]

#sol-item(18, "B", dense: true)[
  A body cell is diploid: 46 chromosomes in 23 pairs.
]

#sol-item(19, "A", dense: true)[
  Mitosis gives two identical cells with the parental chromosome number.
]

#sol-item(20, "C", dense: true)[
  Failure of a chromosome pair to separate at meiosis gives a gamete with two copies of chromosome 21; after fertilisation, three copies are present.
]

#sol-item(21, "B", dense: true)[
  They begin to form in prophase and attach to centromeres at metaphase.
]

#sol-item(22, "D", dense: true)[
  As a cell enlarges, volume increases faster than surface area, so exchange with the environment becomes inadequate.
]

#sol-item(23, "C", dense: true)[
  Telophase rebuilds the nuclei; the chromosomes uncoil and the nuclear membrane re-forms.
]

#sol-item(24, "A", dense: true)[
  Asexual reproduction uses mitosis, so the offspring are clones of the parent.
]

#sol-item(25, "C", dense: true)[
  The four stages in order are prophase, metaphase, anaphase and telophase.
]

#sol-item(26, "B", dense: true)[
  The chromosome number is not changed by replication — there are still 46 chromosomes, each now made of two chromatids.
]

#sol-item(27, "A", dense: true)[
  By halving the number in gametes, meiosis compensates for the doubling that fertilisation would otherwise cause.
]

#sol-item(28, "B", dense: true)[
  Genes, arranged along the DNA of the chromosome, carry the hereditary information.
]

#sol-item(29, "D", dense: true)[
  Malignant tumours invade and metastasise; benign tumours stay where they start.
]

#sol-item(30, "C", dense: true)[
  In unicellular organisms, mitosis is the means of reproduction, giving two identical cells.
]

